The Massachusetts Third Hampshire State Representative District encompasses Amherst and parts of Granby (precincts 1 and 2A), covering 42 square miles with a population of 36,357. The incumbent is Democrat Mindy Domb of Amherst, who has represented the district since winning election in 2018.


